#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# cosh

#% text
# `cosh(x)` gives the hyperbolic cosine `(exp(x) + exp(-x))/2`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `cosh(0)` is 1 and `cosh(-x)` is `cosh(x)`; other exact arguments stay unevaluated.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values. `cosh` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
cosh(0)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
cosh(1.0)
#% output
#= 1.5430806348152437

#% cell
cosh(-2.0)
#% output
#= 3.7621956910836314

#% cell
n(cosh(1), 30)
#% output
#= 1.5430806348152437784779056207570617

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# A hanging chain (catenary) with parameter 2, from `x = -2` to `2`:

#% cell
plot(2*cosh(x/2), [x, -2, 2])
#% output
#= image("cosh.files/cosh-5.svgz")

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The derivative:

#% cell
d(cosh(x), x)
#% output
#= sinh(x)

#% text
# As exponentials:

#% cell
trig_to_exp(cosh(x))
#% output
#= (1/2)*exp(x) + (1/2)*exp(-x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sinh`, `tanh`, `cos`, `exp`
